---
/* L44 - two credentials, a built URL, a nested reply. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L44.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a food van parked at a fenced yard with its serving hatch open, a hose running from the van to a tall pump post with a round dial beside the gate."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L44-fig-title L44-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L44-fig-title">Two credentials build the URL, the reply comes back nested</title>
      <desc id="L44-fig-desc">
        Two small credential boxes on the left - account id and auth token - send two arrows into a tinted box in the middle that shows the endpoint assembled from an account segment and a model segment, with two price chips below it. An arrow leads right into a reply drawn as three nested rectangles: success, result, and answers inside that. A prussian arrow leaves the nested reply, bends down and left, and points at a flat tinted box labelled answers, flat - the shape the rest of the harness sees. The nested layers fade in one after another, then the flattening arrow draws itself.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L44-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect x="36" y="76" width="150" height="42" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="52" y="102" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">account id</text>
      <rect x="36" y="134" width="150" height="42" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="52" y="160" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">auth token</text>
      <text x="36" y="196" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">both, or the adapter says which is missing</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 60; --m-duration: 0.8s;" d="M 186 97 L 232 122" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L44-arrow)" />
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 60; --m-duration: 0.8s; --m-delay: 0.25s;" d="M 186 155 L 232 130" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L44-arrow)" />

      <rect x="236" y="98" width="164" height="80" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="250" y="124" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">accounts/&lt;id&gt;</text>
      <text x="250" y="144" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">ai/run/&lt;model&gt;</text>
      <text x="250" y="166" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">built per account and model</text>

      <rect x="256" y="204" width="62" height="30" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="266" y="224" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.24</text>
      <rect x="330" y="204" width="70" height="30" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="340" y="224" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.038</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 60; --m-duration: 0.8s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" d="M 400 138 L 442 120" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L44-arrow)" />

      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.8s;" x="446" y="60" width="160" height="130" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.8s;" x="460" y="82" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">success</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.05s;" x="462" y="94" width="128" height="82" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.05s;" x="474" y="116" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">result</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.3s;" x="478" y="128" width="96" height="36" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.3s;" x="490" y="151" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">answers</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 128; --m-duration: 1s; --m-delay: 1.5s;" d="M 526 190 L 526 224 L 436 224" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L44-arrow)" />
      <rect x="266" y="244" width="170" height="34" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="280" y="266" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">answers, flat</text>
      <text x="440" y="268" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one shape for every provider</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L44</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Clef needs two credentials, builds its endpoint per account and model, and its nested reply is flattened by the adapter into the one answer shape the harness uses.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
